# Owner-scoped CRUD — educations, experiences, certifications, interests, cvs.
#
# These all hang off a job profile and share one shape: an ability check, then
# `assertProfileScopedListAccess`, then a CASL security query. Swap {{path}} to
# retest another. `cv` has an extra pin, covered in its own section below.

@host = http://localhost:9027/api/v1

# Log in first — REST Client variables do not cross files, so each file does this.
# @name login
POST {{host}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{$dotenv ADMIN_USER_EMAIL}}",
  "password": "{{$dotenv ADMIN_USER_PASSWORD}}"
}

###

@token = {{login.response.body.user.accessToken}}
@path = experiences

### unknown param -> 400. It used to become a $match clause and return nothing.
GET {{host}}/{{path}}?nonsense=x
x-auth-access-token: {{token}}

### undeclared sort -> 400
GET {{host}}/{{path}}?sort=-secretField
x-auth-access-token: {{token}}

### regex metacharacters are escaped, not executed -> 200, empty, no hang
GET {{host}}/{{path}}?clientSearch=(a%2B)%2B%24
x-auth-access-token: {{token}}

### legacy offset paging still works -> totalDocs + totalPages present
GET {{host}}/{{path}}?page=1&limit=5
x-auth-access-token: {{token}}

### cursor page -> nextCursor present, no totalDocs
# @name firstPage
GET {{host}}/{{path}}?limit=5
x-auth-access-token: {{token}}

### follow the cursor — no row may repeat from the previous response
GET {{host}}/{{path}}?limit=5&cursor={{firstPage.response.body.pagination.nextCursor}}
x-auth-access-token: {{token}}

### cursor replayed under a different sort -> 400
GET {{host}}/{{path}}?limit=5&sort=-createdAt&cursor={{firstPage.response.body.pagination.nextCursor}}
x-auth-access-token: {{token}}

###############################################################################
# Scoping — the part that must not have regressed
###############################################################################

### someone else's profile -> 403/404 from assertProfileScopedListAccess,
### never a 200 with their rows. Replace with a real other profile id.
GET {{host}}/{{path}}?jobProfileId=000000000000000000000000
x-auth-access-token: {{token}}

### a malformed jobProfileId is a 400 from Joi, before the access check
GET {{host}}/{{path}}?jobProfileId=nope
x-auth-access-token: {{token}}

### unauthenticated -> 401, never a list
GET {{host}}/{{path}}

###############################################################################
# Per-module filters
###############################################################################

### experiences — enum filters, including the qs bracket shape
GET {{host}}/experiences?workplace=remote&limit=5
x-auth-access-token: {{token}}

GET {{host}}/experiences?employmentType[in][]=full-time&employmentType[in][]=contract
x-auth-access-token: {{token}}

### a value outside the enum -> 400
GET {{host}}/experiences?workplace=not-a-workplace
x-auth-access-token: {{token}}

### date range. `dateRange` coerces to a real Date — a string bound against a
### Date field is type-bracketed by Mongo and would match nothing, silently.
GET {{host}}/experiences?startDate[gte]=2020-01-01&startDate[lte]=2026-12-31
x-auth-access-token: {{token}}

### an unparseable date bound is dropped rather than passed through -> 400 from Joi
GET {{host}}/experiences?startDate[gte]=not-a-date
x-auth-access-token: {{token}}

### educations
GET {{host}}/educations?fieldOfStudy=Computer%20Science&limit=5
x-auth-access-token: {{token}}

### certifications
GET {{host}}/certifications?issuingOrganization=AWS&limit=5
x-auth-access-token: {{token}}

GET {{host}}/certifications?issueDate[gte]=2024-01-01
x-auth-access-token: {{token}}

### interests
GET {{host}}/interests?clientSearch=music&limit=5
x-auth-access-token: {{token}}

### user-interest-surveys — scoped by userId, not jobProfileId
GET {{host}}/user-interest-surveys?isSkipped=false&limit=5
x-auth-access-token: {{token}}

GET {{host}}/user-interest-surveys?clientSearch=design
x-auth-access-token: {{token}}

###############################################################################
# cv — has a pin the others do not
#
# A candidate's CASL rules also match any *published* CV, so the security query
# alone does not keep this list to one person. The controller pins it to the
# profile the access guard authorised. These two must not leak across profiles.
###############################################################################

### own CVs only
GET {{host}}/cvs?limit=100
x-auth-access-token: {{token}}
### expect: every returned jobProfileId is your own

### `jobProfileId` is accepted by the schema but is NOT a spec filter — the pin
### is what scopes the list, so this cannot be used to widen it.
GET {{host}}/cvs?jobProfileId=000000000000000000000000
x-auth-access-token: {{token}}
### expect: 403/404 from the guard, never someone else's CVs

### status filter
GET {{host}}/cvs?status=draft&limit=5
x-auth-access-token: {{token}}

### unknown status -> 400
GET {{host}}/cvs?status=not-a-status
x-auth-access-token: {{token}}
